---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data this site collects, why, and your rights.">
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller of personal data collected through this site is {site.legalTraderName}, {site.author.city}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What is collected and why</h2>
  <p>Reading the site requires no account and collects no personal data beyond what any web server handles. Data is only collected when you choose to use one of the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter</strong> — your email address, the date you subscribed and confirmed (double opt-in), the page you subscribed from, and a topic if the form recorded one. Used only to send the newsletter and, once when you confirm, the download link for the free PDF guide offered to subscribers; every email carries a one-click unsubscribe link, which deletes the address. The download link contains a signed code tied to your address so that it works without an account; downloads are not logged. Legal basis: your consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form</strong> — name, email, the topics you ticked and the text of your message. Used only to answer you, kept only in the mailbox. Legal basis: your request.</li>
    <li><strong>Abuse protection</strong> — to stop forms being flooded, a short-lived counter keyed to a one-way hash of your IP address and email address is kept for up to ten minutes — or up to one day when an address already on the list asks for the PDF link again. The hash cannot be turned back into either value.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</strong> — only when it is switched on, and only after you consent in the cookie banner. Details are in the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Personal data is not sold and is not shared with third parties for marketing.</p>

  <h2>Records of earlier purchases</h2>
  <p>Until {site.shopClosed} some guides were sold as PDF files. For those purchases we keep the records tax and accounting law requires — name, email address, country, amount and date, received from the payment processor Stripe — together with the download log and any review left at the time. Reviews are no longer published, and none of these records is used for anything else. Purchase records are deleted when the retention period ends (currently ten years in Bulgaria); you can ask for your review and download log to be deleted sooner. Legal basis: legal obligation.</p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>The site runs on Cloudflare infrastructure, its data is stored in a Cloudflare database, and emails are sent through Cloudflare. Records of earlier purchases are also held by Stripe. Each is bound by a data-processing agreement.</p>

  <h2>How long</h2>
  <p>Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe; unconfirmed addresses are deleted after ninety days. Contact correspondence is kept as long as it is needed to answer you. Purchase records are kept as described above. You can ask for deletion at any time; we delete everything the law does not require us to keep.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct, delete and restrict the processing of your data, to object, to withdraw consent, and to lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection (CPDP) or your local authority. Requests go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
